<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Obrenović dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1815–1903</span> · Also known as House of Obrenović</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Obrenović dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> from 1815 to 1842 and again from 1858 to 1903. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milos-obrenovic">Miloš Obrenović</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-serbian-uprising">Second Serbian Uprising</a>, it competed for the throne with the Karađorđević family. Under it Serbia won autonomy and then independence, and became a kingdom in 1882. The line ended when King Alexander and Queen Draga were murdered in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/may-coup-serbia">May Coup</a> of 1903.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/obrenovic-dynasty.jpg" alt="Obrenović dynasty" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: House of Obrenović · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Veliki_dvorski_grb_Obrenovi%C4%87a.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
